# What the ComfyUI Registry zip leaves out.
#
# This file ONLY filters the Registry archive. It has no effect on GitHub and
# no effect on a `git clone` install, so anything that must not be published at
# all belongs in .gitignore instead -- the two files are not alternatives.
#
# The rule here is "would a user running this node ever load it?". Development
# tooling would not: it is on GitHub for contributors, and shipping it makes
# every install larger for nothing.

# Test suites and their harnesses.
tests/

# Node tooling for the jsdom suite. node_modules/ is gitignored as well; the
# manifests are not, because CI needs them.
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# Maintainer scripts: the distribution sweep and the audits. The pool lister is
# the one exception -- the README tells every user to run it to see what a pool
# already holds before adding to it, and a Manager install has no other copy.
# comfy-cli matches with pathspec's gitwildmatch, where a later "!" re-includes.
scripts/*
!scripts/builtin_options.py

# Contributor documentation and the README's images. The README itself ships,
# and it references its images by absolute raw.githubusercontent URL precisely
# so it still renders on the Registry page with docs/ left out of the zip.
docs/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
conftest.py

# CI.
.github/

# Caches and local working notes.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.omo/

# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   js/                       -- the frontend; WEB_DIRECTORY serves it at runtime
#   user_options.example.json -- the template users copy to add their own values
#   data/ engine/ nodes/      -- the pack
#   example_workflows/        -- ComfyUI scans this exact name and lists them
#                                under Workflow > Browse Templates
#   LICENSE README.md pyproject.toml
